The CRT step works because the moduli $p_T$ are pairwise coprime (distinct primes), guaranteeing a simultaneous solution. Each subset sum gets its own "private" prime $p_T$ ensuring it's a perfect power of that order — this is the flexibility the previous AI hadn't exploited.

